# The `tests` package (docs/sunit_design.md S1) — the world's own test suites.
#
# A THIRD package beside `world` and `cocoaui`, loaded on top of a booted
# world, so tests can subclass TestCase (world/86_sunit.mst) and name any
# class in the image. Files carry a `t` prefix so this list reads at a glance
# in a shared directory.
#
# It SHIPS in the .app payload on purpose: a fresh install can open the Tests
# tab, press Run All, and watch the library's own suite go green on their own
# machine. No About box makes that argument as well.
#
# Run them: `macvm-gui test`, or `TestRunner runAllAndShow` in a Workspace,
# or `MyTest run` for one class.

# SUnit testing itself. First, because a framework that mis-reports a failure
# says green when it should say red and everything downstream believes it.
t10_sunit_tests.mst
